# forte environment configuration.
#
# Local development is ZERO-CONFIG: with nothing set below, the app uses PGlite
# (PostgreSQL compiled to WASM) in .pglite/ and a development-only auth secret.
# Copy this file to `.env` only when you need non-default values.
#
# All variables are validated by lib/env.ts. Values that are present are always
# checked for shape; the three marked REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION additionally make a
# production server refuse to start when missing (assertProductionEnv(), called
# from instrumentation.ts).

# --- Runtime ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Set by Next.js automatically. Listed for completeness.
# NODE_ENV="development"

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset  -> PGlite in .pglite/ (no server, no connection string).
# Set    -> lib/db.ts switches to the `pg` driver against this connection string.
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. Must be a postgres:// or postgresql:// URL.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/forte"

# --- Authentication (Better Auth) ------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. Token signing secret, minimum 32 characters.
# A weak development-only fallback ("forte-dev-secret") is used when unset
# outside production and must never be relied on for real data.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""

# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. Absolute origin used for callbacks and redirects,
# e.g. https://forte.example.com — no trailing slash.
# When unset locally, Better Auth derives the origin from the incoming request.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=""
